  "title": "The Ice-Cube Post Office",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "block-world chain reactions",
  "premise": "A square courier must send three sealed parcels across a model ice shelf, but a single frozen conveyor is locked. Warm-colored fantasy tiles thaw one latch at a time, letting the conveyor advance in short sections until the parcels reach insulated nests and the courier receives a thank-you snowflake.",
  "hook": "The mail route has frozen mid-sentence.",
  "visible_action": "Glow tiles light in sequence; transparent latches soften; belt sections advance; parcels settle into nests; a snowflake card unfolds.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A stalled process can be restarted section by section.",
  "gate": "Explicit fantasy thaw tiles; no claim about real ice melting rates, refrigeration, or mail handling.",
